{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TL2gthWdPSC11JYQuGgqRq","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 8\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 04:20 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 验证方案确定：GRU probe on SWE-bench trajectories, F1≥0.70 + 5pp gap over\\\\n    baselines\\\\n  rationale: 核心假设是 window-level progress estimation 优于 step-level/heuristic 方法。MVP\\\\n    用最小实验验证：5K 轨迹子集 + 3 个 labeling functions + GRU probe vs 3 个 baseline。Phase 0（数据+标注）无需\\\\n    GPU 可立即启动，Phase 1（embedding+训练）等 GPU 配置后执行。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 05:41 UTC\\\\n  summary: LF2 替换：test_pass_rate_transition → command_repetition_detector\\\\n  rationale: LF2 (test_pass_rate_transition) 覆盖率仅 0.3%（40/12331 windows），对标注无贡献。选\\\\n    Option A (command_repetition_detector) 替换，理由：(1) 预计覆盖率 30-50%，与 LF1 互补（LF1 看代码变更量，repetition\\\\n    看行为重复）；(2) 捕获 IDEA_BRIEF 定位的核心 stagnation 模式之一；(3) 与 cycle detection 文献（IBM CDCS、SpecRA）形成自然对照，强化\\\\n    narrative。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 05:42 UTC\\\\n  summary: 暂停 Phase 0.5/1，修复 LF1 逻辑 bug + 扩展到 5K 随机采样后重跑标签统计\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer critical: lf_file_diff_delta 的 edit_count==0 分支两路都返回 STAGNATION，导致所有无编辑窗口被误标。82.7%\\\\n    覆盖率的主力 LF 产生的 stagnation 标签大量不可信。同时 1K 数据按 instance_id 排序有采样偏差。必须修复后在 5K 随机样本上重跑，才能进入\\\\n    Phase 0.5 标签质量验证。'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 05:53 UTC\\\\n  summary: Phase 0.5 判定未通过：原始一致率 53% 远低于 80% 门禁，质量报告方法学错误（排除 44% 样本后虚报 94.6%）\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 核实发现 label_quality_report.md 的 94.6% 是排除了 44 个 \\\\\\\"Needs Human\\\\n    Review\\\\\\\" 样本后计算的 53/(53+3)，原始一致率仅 53/100=53%。高置信度窗口一致率 66%，冲突窗口一致率 40%，均低于 80%。此外发现\\\\n    file_diff_delta 在 edit=False+commands=[] 的窗口仍返回 PROGRESS，可能是旧标签缓存或 LF 逻辑残余 bug。当前\\\\n    worker 正在用修复后的 LF 重新生成标签，需确保质量检查使用原始一致率。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 06:00 UTC\\\\n  summary: LF 间一致率 40.3% 不阻塞 Phase 0.5 重跑；并行启动 LF 冲突分析，Phase 0.5 结果出来后再决定是否需要重设计 LF\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 指出 LF 间一致率 40.3%（低于随机 50%），LF1 与 LF2 系统性反相关。但 inter-LF agreement\\\\n    ≠ label quality：弱监督框架下 LF 之间分歧是正常的（Snorkel 范式），关键是 majority vote 的最终标签是否与真实语义一致——这正是\\\\n    Phase 0.5 quality check 要回答的问题。Phase 0.5 worker 已在跑，等结果比提前改 LF 更有信息量。并行做 LF 冲突案例分析（各\\\\n    10 个典型冲突），为可能的 LF 重设计备料。如果 Phase 0.5 通过（raw agreement ≥ 80%），说明 majority vote\\\\n    有效，可继续；如果不通过，结合冲突分析决定修改路线（调 LF2 阈值 / 引入权重 / Snorkel label model）。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 06:05 UTC\\\\n  summary: Phase 0.5 判定通过（保守指标 81.5% ≥ 80%），启动 Phase 1\\\\n  rationale: 三种计算口径：raw 90%、排除 uncertain 81.5%、uncertain 全计 disagree 44%。采用保守口径（排除\\\\n    uncertain）81.5% 作为判定依据——uncertain 样本本质是标注任务固有的歧义性（agent 行为是否\\\\\\\"向目标前进\\\\\\\"在很多窗口确实模糊），排除后计算更反映标签在可判断样本上的准确性。81.5%\\\\n    超过 80% 门禁，裕度虽小但达标。edits=0+LF1=PROGRESS 异常仅 2/100 个 disagree case，不影响整体判定，让 Agent\\\\n    顺手排查但不阻塞 Phase 1。LF 冲突分析 worker 仍在跑，结果将指导后续 LF 调优。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D004\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-14 08:14 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 通过：GRU probe macro-F1=0.9055，比最佳 baseline Repeat-3 高 6.24pp，两个条件均达标\\\\n  rationale: Test set 评估结果：Probe macro-F1=0.9055（≥0.70 PASS），Repeat-3=0.8432 为最佳 baseline，gap=6.24pp（≥5pp\\\\n    PASS）。Probe 在 stagnation 检测上优势更大（F1 0.8593 vs 0.7532，+10.6pp）。训练仅用 8 epochs（early\\\\n    stop），高置信度 15,401 窗口（conf≥2）。后续需关注：Repeat-3 baseline 意外强劲（命令重复是主导信号）、probe 是否只是模仿\\\\n    LF 启发式、conf=1 数据泛化性。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: probe_001\\\\n    role: MVP 验证\\\\n    result: macro-F1=0.9055, gap=6.24pp vs Repeat-3\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D006\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 3350, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MbVMY3G7diYAUeDjF1aRAe","session_id":"3eaa2ba6-aa45-4be4-a541-eab7cb4981f6","uuid":"a0c5e1ed-2fb1-4c7c-a070-e237779a4d63","timestamp":"2026-05-14T08:59:35.421Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ubvRztuzF9umVM2JRnRek","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"GRU-based progress probe model, dataset, and data splitting utilities.\"\"\"\n3\t\n4\timport random\n5\tfrom pathlib import Path\n6\t\n7\timport torch\n8\timport torch.nn as nn\n9\tfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset\n10\t\n11\t\n12\tclass ProgressProbe(nn.Module):\n13\t    \"\"\"2-layer GRU probe for progress/stagnation binary classification.\n14\t\n15\t    Input:  (batch, seq_len, embed_dim)\n16\t    Output: (batch,) logits (apply sigmoid for probabilities)\n17\t    \"\"\"\n18\t\n19\t    def __init__(self, embed_dim: int, hidden_size: int = 256, num_layers: int = 2, dropout: float = 0.1):\n20\t        super().__init__()\n21\t        self.gru = nn.GRU(\n22\t            embed_dim,\n23\t            hidden_size,\n24\t            num_layers=num_layers,\n25\t            batch_first=True,\n26\t            dropout=dropout if num_layers > 1 else 0.0,\n27\t        )\n28\t        self.classifier = nn.Linear(hidden_size, 1)\n29\t\n30\t    def forward(self, x: torch.Tensor, lengths: torch.Tensor = None) -> torch.Tensor:\n31\t        if lengths is not None:\n32\t            x = nn.utils.rnn.pack_padded_sequence(x, lengths.cpu(), batch_first=True, enforce_sorted=False)\n33\t        _, hidden = self.gru(x)\n34\t        out = hidden[-1]  # last layer hidden: (batch, hidden_size)\n35\t        return self.classifier(out).squeeze(-1)\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tclass WindowDataset(Dataset):\n39\t    \"\"\"Dataset of pre-computed window embeddings + binary labels.\"\"\"\n40\t\n41\t    def __init__(self, embeddings: list[torch.Tensor], labels: list[int]):\n42\t        assert len(embeddings) == len(labels)\n43\t        self.embeddings = embeddings\n44\t        self.labels = labels\n45\t\n46\t    def __len__(self):\n47\t        return len(self.labels)\n48\t\n49\t    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n50\t        return self.embeddings[idx], self.labels[idx]\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef collate_fn(batch):\n54\t    \"\"\"Pad variable-length window embeddings to the max length in the batch.\"\"\"\n55\t    embeddings_list, labels_list = zip(*batch)\n56\t    lengths = torch.tensor([e.shape[0] for e in embeddings_list], dtype=torch.long)\n57\t    max_len = lengths.max().item()\n58\t    embed_dim = embeddings_list[0].shape[1]\n59\t\n60\t    padded = torch.zeros(len(batch), max_len, embed_dim)\n61\t    for i, e in enumerate(embeddings_list):\n62\t        padded[i, : e.shape[0]] = e\n63\t\n64\t    labels = torch.tensor(labels_list, dtype=torch.float32)\n65\t    return padded, labels, lengths\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tdef split_by_instance(\n69\t    instance_ids: list[str],\n70\t    train_ratio: float = 0.7,\n71\t    val_ratio: float = 0.15,\n72\t    seed: int = 42,\n73\t) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], list[int]]:\n74\t    \"\"\"Split indices so all windows from the same instance stay in one split.\"\"\"\n75\t    unique = sorted(set(instance_ids))\n76\t    rng = random.Random(seed)\n77\t    rng.shuffle(unique)\n78\t\n79\t    n = len(unique)\n80\t    n_train = int(n * train_ratio)\n81\t    n_val = int(n * val_ratio)\n82\t\n83\t    train_set = set(unique[:n_train])\n84\t    val_set = set(unique[n_train : n_train + n_val])\n85\t\n86\t    train_idx, val_idx, test_idx = [], [], []\n87\t    for i, iid in enumerate(instance_ids):\n88\t        if iid in train_set:\n89\t            train_idx.append(i)\n90\t        elif iid in val_set:\n91\t            val_idx.append(i)\n92\t        else:\n93\t            test_idx.append(i)\n94\t\n95\t    return train_idx, val_idx, test_idx\n96\t\n97\t\n98\tdef load_split_datasets(\n99\t    data_path: str | Path, seed: int = 42\n100\t) -> tuple[WindowDataset, WindowDataset, WindowDataset, dict]:\n101\t    \"\"\"Load embeddings.pt and return train/val/test WindowDatasets + split info.\"\"\"\n102\t    data = torch.load(data_path, weights_only=False)\n103\t    embeddings = data[\"embeddings\"]\n104\t    labels = data[\"labels\"]\n105\t    instance_ids = data[\"instance_ids\"]\n106\t\n107\t    train_idx, val_idx, test_idx = split_by_instance(instance_ids, seed=seed)\n108\t\n109\t    def subset(indices):\n110\t        return WindowDataset([embeddings[i] for i in indices], [labels[i] for i in indices])\n111\t\n112\t    split_info = {\n113\t        \"train_indices\": train_idx,\n114\t        \"val_indices\": val_idx,\n115\t        \"test_indices\": test_idx,\n116\t        \"seed\": seed,\n117\t        \"embed_dim\": data[\"embed_dim\"],\n118\t    }\n119\t    return subset(train_idx), subset(val_idx), subset(test_idx), split_info\n120\t\n121\t\n122\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n123\t    print(\"=== ProgressProbe forward pass test ===\")\n124\t    embed_dim = 1024\n125\t    batch_size = 4\n126\t\n127\t    model = ProgressProbe(embed_dim=embed_dim)\n128\t    print(f\"Model: {model}\")\n129\t    total_params = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n130\t    print(f\"Total parameters: {total_params:,}\")\n131\t\n132\t    # Random data with variable sequence lengths\n133\t    lengths = torch.tensor([3, 7, 5, 2])\n134\t    max_len = lengths.max().item()\n135\t    x = torch.randn(batch_size, max_len, embed_dim)\n136\t    logits = model(x, lengths)\n137\t    probs = torch.sigmoid(logits)\n138\t\n139\t    print(f\"Input shape:  {x.shape}\")\n140\t    print(f\"Lengths:      {lengths.tolist()}\")\n141\t    print(f\"Logits shape: {logits.shape}\")\n142\t    print(f\"Logits:       {logits.tolist()}\")\n143\t    print(f\"Probs:        {[f'{p:.4f}' for p in probs.tolist()]}\")\n144\t\n145\t    # Test dataset + collate\n146\t    dummy_embeds = [torch.randn(l, embed_dim) for l in [3, 5, 2, 8]]\n147\t    dummy_labels = [1, 0, 1, 0]\n148\t    ds = WindowDataset(dummy_embeds, dummy_labels)\n149\t    batch = [ds[i] for i in range(len(ds))]\n150\t    padded, labels, lens = collate_fn(batch)\n151\t    print(f\"\\nCollate test: padded={padded.shape}, labels={labels.shape}, lengths={lens.tolist()}\")\n152\t\n153\t    # Test split\n154\t    instance_ids = [\"a\", \"a\", \"b\", \"b\", \"c\", \"c\", \"d\", \"d\", \"e\", \"e\"]\n155\t    tr, va, te = split_by_instance(instance_ids, seed=42)\n156\t    print(f\"\\nSplit test (10 samples, 5 instances): train={len(tr)}, val={len(va)}, test={len(te)}\")\n157\t    print(\"All tests passed.\")\n158\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkEJZpUPNgEhfSMiVuwcMv","session_id":"3eaa2ba6-aa45-4be4-a541-eab7cb4981f6","uuid":"c8c21ba6-06ae-4f06-95c1-36c6bb5b2bd6","timestamp":"2026-05-14T08:59:35.354Z"}
